\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Phase 1: Validation accuracy over 50 federated rounds} (mean across 3 seeds). Left column: IID; right column: non-IID (Dirichlet $\alpha {=}0.5$). Rows: HomeOccupancy, HomeHAR, MNIST, CIFAR-10. All algorithms use uniform tier distribution (35\%~S/35\%~M/30\%~L). HomeHAR curves collapse to the majority-class baseline (${\approx }31\%$), revealing a dataset-level challenge independent of algorithm choice. On HomeOccupancy IID, FedMKS and FedAvg match the centralised ceiling; under non-IID, weight-sharing methods degrade sharply while Local and FedMD remain more robust. On MNIST, all FL methods approach centralised accuracy under IID; non-IID separates FedMKS/FedAvg/FedProx from FedMD/FedAKD/Local. On CIFAR-10, the task difficulty suppresses all federated methods by $>10\%$ relative to Central, underscoring the limits of knowledge distillation with small per-client datasets. \dag  ~FedAKD and FedMKS curves on HomeOccupancy non-IID terminated early (16 and 20 rounds respectively) due to training instability.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:phase1}{{4}{6}{}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Phase 2 placeholder.} Validation accuracy of FedMD under three tier-heterogeneity configurations (\texttt  {all\_small}, \texttt  {uniform}, \texttt  {skewed}) on HomeOccupancy IID and non-IID. Results to be added.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:phase2}{{5}{6}{}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Phase 3 placeholder.} Validation accuracy and efficiency metrics (server compute, client compute, communication bytes per round) for FedMKS vs.\ FedDF on HomeOccupancy and HomeHAR under IID and non-IID data partitions. Results to be added.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:phase3}{{6}{6}{}{figure.6}{}}
